  "synopsis": [
    {
      "langue": "en",
      "text": "Based on the board game, the object is to guess either a word or phrase based on a drawing. Each team starts on the same square on the board and the first team attempts to draw a picture based on a clue.  If his team correctly guesses the clue, then this team gets to roll the dice and advance along the board.  If the team fails to guess correctly, then the other team gets a chance to draw and guess. The game plays much in this way until a team reaches the final square on the board and successfully guesses the clue to win the game.\n\nThis game contains three different modes; regular game, alternative game, and drawing practice. It also allows for up to four teams which can be made comprising of any number of players per each team. \n\nIn the regular game, a team will be given a turn to start revealing pieces of one of the 500+ drawings that are hidden in the game. Each drawing is a 6x8 size and has 48 pieces to it. To reveal the pieces, the player is made to play one of four timed minigames which are chosen depending on the color of the square the player landed on the board. The minigames consist of Attack of the Paint Zombies, The WareHouse Shuffle, Leapin' Energy Capsules!, and Four Alarm Rescue. In Attack of the Paint Zombies the player fires downwards at the aliens and the more aliens that are hit the more pieces that are revealed of the drawing. If the aliens hit the player, the player loses time off the clock. In The WareHouse Shuffle, the player goes all the way to the left side and then stacks as many boxes on top of each other that they can bring over all the way to the right side. While transporting the boxes, their are two enemies who can hit into your boxes thus subtracting them from the haul and also taking time away. Each box brought over reduces a piece of the hidden drawing. In  Leapin' Energy Capsules!, the player is an astronaut and is moving and jumping to collect blue spheres. While collecting the spheres the player must try to avoid hitting any enemies which will reduce time. Each sphere collected clears up another piece of the drawing. In Four Alarm Rescue, the player controls a pair of firemen on the ground with a net who are moving back and forth catching the jumping people above on the net. Each person rescued leads a revealed piece of the drawing while each person not rescued leads to reduced time.\n\nThe alternative game allows the player to draw the picture for other players to guess, so their are no minigames in this mode. Other than that, it is the same as the regular mode.\n\nDrawing practice lets the player practice their drawing technique without the pressure of a timer."
    },
    {
      "langue": "fr",
      "text": "Pictionary est un jeu de plateau développé par Software Creations et publié par LJN sur NES. Il est basé sur le jeu de société du même nom, les joueurs peuvent jouer jusqu'à quatre équipes de joueurs illimités."
    },
    {
      "langue": "de",
      "text": "In Anlehnung an das Brettspiel geht es darum, anhand einer Zeichnung entweder ein Wort oder einen Satz zu erraten. Jedes Team beginnt auf demselben Feld auf dem Spielbrett und das erste Team versucht, ein Bild auf der Grundlage eines Hinweises zu zeichnen. Wenn sein Team den Hinweis richtig errät, darf es würfeln und auf dem Spielbrett vorrücken. Wenn das Team nicht richtig rät, bekommt das andere Team die Chance zu zeichnen und zu raten. Das Spiel läuft so lange, bis ein Team das letzte Feld auf dem Spielbrett erreicht und den letzten Hinweis richtig errät, um das Spiel zu gewinnen.\r\n\r\nDieses Spiel enthält drei verschiedene Modi: normales Spiel, alternatives Spiel und Zeichenübung. Bei der alternativen Spielvariante gibt es im Gegensatz zum normalen Spiel keine Minispiele. Mit der Zeichenübung kann der Spieler seine Zeichentechnik ohne den Druck eines Timers üben. In den ersten beiden Modi können bis zu vier Teams gebildet werden, die aus einer beliebigen Anzahl von Spielern pro Team bestehen können."
    },
    {
      "langue": "es",
      "text": "Basado en el juego de mesa, el objetivo es adivinar una palabra o frase basada en un dibujo. Cada equipo comienza en el mismo cuadrado del tablero y el primer equipo intenta dibujar una imagen basándose en una pista. Si su equipo adivina correctamente la pista, este equipo puede tirar los dados y avanzar a lo largo del tablero. Si el equipo no adivina correctamente, entonces el otro equipo tiene la oportunidad de dibujar y adivinar. El juego termina hasta que un equipo alcanza la casilla final en el tablero y adivina con éxito la pista para ganar el juego.\r\nEste juego contiene tres modos diferentes; Juego regular, juego alternativo y práctica de dibujo. También permite hasta cuatro equipos, que pueden conformarse con cualquier número de jugadores por equipo."
    },
    {
      "langue": "it",
      "text": "Pictionary è un gioco da tavolo sviluppato da Software Creations e pubblicato da LJN per NES. Si basa sul gioco da tavolo con lo stesso nome, i giocatori possono giocare fino a quattro squadre di giocatori illimitati."
    },
    {
      "langue": "pt",
      "text": "Pictionary é um jogo de tabuleiro desenvolvido pela Software Creations e publicado pela LJN no NES. É baseado no jogo de tabuleiro de mesmo nome, os jogadores podem jogar até quatro times de jogadores ilimitados."
    }
  ],
